 easily and was expected to challenge Nakatani, based on his performance. But in the quarter-finals, Nakatani threw Maruyam for " [:em {} "ippon"] " in only 24 seconds. In the semi-final, Nakatani faced the Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/34406"} "Oleg Stepanov"] " who had fought him to a decision only the year before. But in Tokyo, Nakatani threw Stepanov twice for " [:em {} "waza-ari"] ", winning in 4:25. The other semi-final was won by the Swiss, " [:a {:href "/athletes/33850"} "Eric Hänni"] ". The final was unusual. Nakatani gained a " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " early in the match. After one minute of combat, Nakatani pulled Hänni off his feet with " [:em {} "de-ashi-barai"] ", but it was ignored by the referee. Suddenly the judges stopped the contest, and began a long discussion with the referee. While the crowd grew restless, suddenly the referee declared another " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " for the " [:em {} "de-ashi-barai"] " and gave the decision to Nakatani."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34125"} "Takehide Nakatani"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/33850"} "Eric Hänni"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34406"} "Oleg Stepanov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "